From: rnsbox <rnsbox@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] licheervnano-rv64: reclock the uarts — exact 2 Mbaud SLIP

The LicheeRV Nano arm64 and rv64 board dts inherited soph_base's uarts
verbatim: 8250 with a hardcoded clock-frequency of 25 MHz (FSBL sets
clk_cam0_200 to 25 MHz at power-on). The SLIP link to the HaLow modem
therefore topped out at 1,562,500 baud and the shipped default was
1500000.

Reclock the SoC once, in of_clk_init before any driver probes:
disppll 1188 -> 768 MHz (needs the enabled LUT row), clk_cam0_200 ->
disppll/8 = 96 MHz. Every dw-uart is a gate-only child of clk_cam0_200,
so the 8250 input becomes 96 MHz and the modem's factory 2 Mbaud is
exact (96M/16/3). &uart1 already takes its rate from the CCF and is
enabled; the pinmux for XGPIOA[28]/[29] is already programmed by the
board's u-boot cvi_board_init.c.
diff --git a/build/boards/sg200x/sg2002_licheervnano_sd/dts_riscv/sg2002_licheervnano_sd.dts b/build/boards/sg200x/sg2002_licheervnano_sd/dts_riscv/sg2002_licheervnano_sd.dts
index e4eff4f..cdcacb6 100644
--- a/build/boards/sg200x/sg2002_licheervnano_sd/dts_riscv/sg2002_licheervnano_sd.dts
+++ b/build/boards/sg200x/sg2002_licheervnano_sd/dts_riscv/sg2002_licheervnano_sd.dts
@@ -80,6 +80,18 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+// RNSBox: reclock disppll 1188 -> 768 MHz and clk_cam0_200 osc/1 ->
+// disppll/8 = 96 MHz (of_clk_init, before any driver probes). Every
+// dw-uart is a gate-only child of clk_cam0_200, so the 8250 input
+// becomes 96 MHz: 2 Mbaud is exact (96M/16/3), 1 Mbaud too (quot 6).
+// The 768 MHz rate needs the enabled LUT entry in the clk driver (this
+// series); without the reclock the SLIP ceiling stays at 1,562,500.
+&clk {
+	assigned-clocks = <&clk CV181X_CLK_DISPPLL>, <&clk CV181X_CLK_CAM0_200>;
+	assigned-clock-parents = <0>, <&clk CV181X_CLK_DISPPLL>;
+	assigned-clock-rates = <768000000>, <96000000>;
+};
+
 &pwm0 {
         status = "okay";
 };
